 "A car is identified by its appearance record, not its file name - 352 of 540 cars differ between the two. rr3mods.json remembers which side each car is on; the path is below, because the game folder itself is usually read-only and the file cannot live there.": [
  "MainWindow"
 ],
 "A car's own pages are named the way its models are: misc.png becomes <car>_misc, wheel.png becomes <car>_wheel. Pick a picture for a slot and it is converted to the texture format chosen in Settings when you press Save - not when you pick it.": [
  "MainWindow",
  "DetailPane",
  "CarsPage"
 ],
 "A manager for Real Racing 3 car mods: it reads the game's own tables so it can tell a car you made from one that shipped, keeps the three asset manifests honest after every edit, and pushes the result to a device over adb.": [
  "MainWindow"
 ],
 "A material with no slot in liveryStringTable.bin.nct cannot be named by any car, so it never appears in the Parts or Paints dropdowns. This box hides those.": [
  "MainWindow"
 ],
 "A mesh whose name is not in the string table is skipped by the engine - the log calls it an unreferenced mesh. The game keeps a per-car list of part names, so an invented name can never be drawn; borrowing a shipped name this car leaves empty gives the part an identity the engine already knows. Rename the mesh in Blender to the name shown here.": [
  "MainWindow",
  "DetailPane",
  "CarsPage"
 ],
 "A new car gets its own figures whether or not you tick this. When modifying a car that is already installed the numbers are left alone unless you ask, because a spec edit is easy to make and hard to notice afterwards.": [
  "BuildDialog"
 ],
 "A new car with no series is a car the game cannot offer you: it sits in the showroom and nothing runs it. Tick the box to have one made for it in a menu group of its own, running the same races as the template. Leave it alone to add the car without touching the career file.": [
  "BuildDialog"
 ],
 "A pack is one file holding the files and the list of what has to be there before they work. The list is checked when someone opens the pack, not when they install it, so a missing driver pose is a sentence rather than a car with no driver in it.": [
  "MainWindow"
 ],
 "A pack somebody sent you": [
  "MainWindow"
 ],
 "A page in vehicles/common is shared: the tyres, discs, glass and interior weaves every car can point at. Changing one changes every car that names it, so a page is only deleted when this program brought it and nothing names it any more.": [
  "MainWindow"
 ],
 "A PNG or JPEG; it is resized to the size the game's own cards use": [
